{"mode": "PINNED", "item_index": 21, "content": "Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. The coordinator divides 36 plain badges equally among 6 volunteers. To find out how many badges each volunteer gets, we divide 36 by 6:\n36 \u00f7 6 = 6\n\nSo each volunteer gets 6 plain badges.\n\n2. Each volunteer then receives 4 extra badges from a separate reserve. To find out how many badges each volunteer has now, we add the 6 plain badges to the 4 extra badges:\n6 + 4 = 10\n\nSo each volunteer has 10 badges after receiving the extra badges.\n\nANSWER: 10", "cost_usd": 6.88e-06, "credit_only": true}
